ParDRe-MR
---------

ParDRe-MR is a parallel MapReduce-based tool to remove duplicate reads.
Duplicate reads can be seen as identical or nearly identical sequences 
with some mismatches. This tool allows the users to avoid the analysis 
of not necessary reads, reducing the time of subsequent procedures with 
the dataset (e.g., assemblies, mappings, etc.).

More info at http://pardremr.des.udc.es


Quick User's Guide
------------------

- Prerequisites

1) Make sure you have Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.7 or above

2) Make sure you have a working Hadoop distribution version 2.4 or above

	2.1) HADOOP_HOME environmental variable must be set accordingly

3) Set PARDREMR_HOME environmental variable:

	3.1) On UNIX/Linux/Mac you can set them in your profile or your 
	shell configuration files, please just follow the instructions
        below:

	export PARDREMR_HOME=/path/to/pardremr/
        export PATH=$PARDREMR_HOME/bin:$PATH


- Execution:

The following command removes the duplicates of identical reads (no mis-
matches) of a single-end dataset and prefix length of 15:

	$ pardre-mr -i dataset.fastq -l 15

The following command shows a similar example but for paired-end computing,
allowing two mismatches and with prefix length of 20:

	$ pardre-mr -i dataset1.fastq -p dataset2.fastq -m 2

